@ 2 0 0 16515594e583e0c30108b6580c323c7e
+       /** Pull the capture sets of an intersection out of it, as their meet:
+        *  `A^{CV_1} & B^{CV_2}` becomes `(A & B)^{CV_1 ** CV_2}`. `normalizeCaptures` does
+        *  not do this, since the meet of two sets whose elements are known only later can
+        *  come out too small during Setup. It is done where an inferred intersection is the
+        *  type of one value which is checked as a whole: an instance of an anonymous class
+        *  with several parents, which is an intersection of them, and a parameter of a
+        *  closure, which takes its type from the function type expected. Both sets are
+        *  then variables this map has just made, so nothing is decided before they are
+        *  filled in. Without the rewrite the value keeps a capture set for each operand,
+        *  and conforms neither to the same intersection with one capture set nor to what
+        *  `unsafeAssumePure` strips. Other inferred intersections are left alone: the
+        *  type of a variable bound by a typed pattern is the scrutinee's meeting the
+        *  pattern's, and the two are checked separately.
+        */
+       def meetCaptures(tp: Type): Type = tp match
+         case AndType(tp1 @ CapturingType(parent1, refs1), tp2 @ CapturingType(parent2, refs2))
+         if meetIntersections && tp1.isBoxed == tp2.isBoxed && !refs1.isConst && !refs2.isConst =>
+           CapturingType(AndType(parent1, parent2), refs1 ** refs2, tp1.isBoxed)
+         case _ => tp
+

